## PHASE 2 — BUILD THIS NOW
Work from builds/dungeon-x-phaser.html (the Phaser 3 version).
Reference the game bible for ALL design decisions.

### Priority 1: D&D 5e Combat System
- Attack rolls: d20 + modifier vs target AC. Miss = miss (no guaranteed damage)
- Four damage types: Physical, Fire, Ice, Lightning (enemies have resistances)
- Initiative: d20 + DEX modifier, higher goes first
- Saving throws: STR/DEX/CON/INT/WIS/CHA, DC = 8 + modifier
- Death: HP hits 0 = dead. Permadeath. Reset to tavern with nothing.
- See docs/combat-system-dnd.md for full stat blocks

### Priority 2: Class Selection (4 classes)
- **Fighter:** STR 16, CON 14, DEX 12. Heavy armor (AC 18). Power Strike (2x damage, 3/rest). Shield Wall (+2 AC, 1 turn). Cleave (hit adjacent enemy on kill).
- **Ranger:** DEX 16, WIS 14, STR 12. Medium armor (AC 15). Twin Shot (2 arrows). Trap Set (1d8 on trigger). Track (reveals enemies 1 room ahead for 5 turns).
- **Mage:** INT 16, WIS 14, DEX 10. No armor (AC 12). Fireball (3d6 area). Frost Nova (1d6 + slow). Lightning Bolt (4d6 line). Shield (absorb 10 HP). Mana pool: 20, regen 2/turn.
- **Cleric:** WIS 16, CON 14, STR 12. Medium armor (AC 16). Heal (2d8+WIS). Smite (2d6 radiant). Turn Undead (flee 3 turns). Bless (+2 attack for 5 turns). 15 mana, regen 1/turn.
- Class selection screen at game start, before entering tavern

### Priority 3: Multi-Floor Dungeon System
- Dungeon 1: Whispering Crypts (2 floors). See game bible Section 5.1.
- Floor transitions: staircase tiles. Going down = new floor generated.
- Each floor: 5-8 rooms connected by corridors. Procedural layout.
- Rooms contain: enemies, treasure, traps, puzzles, boss rooms (floor 2)
- Mini-boss on Floor 1: Vault Warden (AC 16, HP 45, shield mechanic)
- Dungeon boss on Floor 2: Crypt Lord (AC 18, HP 80, raise dead ability)
- Fragment of Dawn in boss room after defeating Crypt Lord

### Priority 4: Overworld Path
- Simple path from Thornhaven (tavern) to dungeon entrance
- Random encounter chance on path (25% per tile)
- Path enemies: weaker than dungeon enemies (Wolves, Bandits, Giant Spiders)
- Visual: grassy tiles, trees, road. Day/night cycle (cosmetic only)

### Priority 5: Daily Seeded Dungeons
- Use date string as seed: "2026-03-09" → deterministic RNG
- Same seed = same layout, same enemies, same loot for all players
- Leaderboard: fastest clear time stored in localStorage
- New seed every day at midnight

## Architecture Rules
- Game state object: { player, inventory, dungeon, floor, reputation, fragments[], dailySeed }
- Scene management: TitleScene → ClassSelectScene → TavernScene → OverworldScene → DungeonScene → CombatScene
- Combat is turn-based: player action → enemy action → repeat
- Inventory: 4x6 grid (24 slots) + 6 equipment slots (head, chest, legs, weapon, offhand, ring)
- All enemy stat blocks in the game bible are CANON — use exact numbers

## Build Rules
- Output to builds/dungeon-x-phase2.html
- Keep Phase 1 build intact (don't overwrite)
- ONE HTML file. All JS inline or in <script> tags.
- Phaser 3 patterns: use Scenes, GameObjects, Tilemaps, Input events
- Test every change in browser. Must not crash on load.
- Performance: target 60fps on M4 Mac, 30fps minimum on mobile Safari
- No external assets — draw everything programmatically (rectangles, circles, text)
- Color palette: dark fantasy (deep purples, warm torchlight oranges, cool stone grays)
- Font: monospace for all text (16px for UI, 12px for tooltips)

